#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The phase estimation problem {#the-phase-estimation-problem}"
msgstr "Masalah estimasi fase {#the-phase-estimation-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This section of the lesson explains the *phase estimation problem*.\n"
"We'll begin with a short discussion of the *spectral theorem* from linear algebra, and then move on to a statement of the phase estimation problem itself.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bagian pelajaran ini menjelaskan *masalah estimasi fase*.\n"
"Kita akan mulai dengan diskusi singkat tentang *teorema spektral* dari aljabar linear, kemudian beralih ke pernyataan masalah estimasi fase itu sendiri.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Spectral theorem {#spectral-theorem}"
msgstr "Teorema spektral {#spectral-theorem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The *spectral theorem* is an important fact from linear algebra that states that matrices of a certain type, called *normal matrices,* can be expressed in a simple and useful way.\n"
"We'll only need this theorem for unitary matrices in this lesson, but down the road in this series we'll apply it to Hermitian matrices as well.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Teorema spektral* adalah fakta penting dari aljabar linear yang menyatakan bahwa matriks dari jenis tertentu, yang disebut *matriks normal,* dapat dinyatakan dengan cara yang sederhana dan berguna.\n"
"Kita hanya akan membutuhkan teorema ini untuk matriks uniter dalam pelajaran ini, tetapi di masa mendatang dalam seri ini kita akan menerapkannya pada matriks Hermitian juga.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Normal matrices {#normal-matrices}"
msgstr "Matriks normal {#normal-matrices}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A square matrix $M$ with complex number entries is said to be a *normal* matrix if it commutes with its conjugate transpose:\n"
"$M M^{\\dagger} = M^{\\dagger} M.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Matriks persegi $M$ dengan entri bilangan kompleks dikatakan sebagai matriks *normal* jika ia komut dengan transpos konjugatnya:\n"
"$M M^{\\dagger} = M^{\\dagger} M.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Every unitary matrix $U$ is normal because\n"
msgstr "Setiap matriks uniter $U$ adalah normal karena\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U U^{\\dagger} = \\mathbb{I} = U^{\\dagger} U.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U U^{\\dagger} = \\mathbb{I} = U^{\\dagger} U.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Hermitian matrices, which are matrices that equal their own conjugate transpose, are another important class of normal matrices.\n"
"If $H$ is a Hermitian matrix, then\n"
msgstr ""
"Matriks Hermitian, yang merupakan matriks yang sama dengan transpos konjugatnya sendiri, adalah kelas penting lain dari matriks normal.\n"
"Jika $H$ adalah matriks Hermitian, maka\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H H^{\\dagger} = H^2 = H^{\\dagger} H,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H H^{\\dagger} = H^2 = H^{\\dagger} H,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "so $H$ is normal.\n"
msgstr "sehingga $H$ adalah normal.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Not every square matrix is normal.\n"
"For instance, this matrix isn't normal:\n"
msgstr ""
"Tidak setiap matriks persegi adalah normal.\n"
"Misalnya, matriks ini tidak normal:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(This is a simple but great example of a matrix that's often very helpful to consider.)\n"
"It isn't normal because\n"
msgstr ""
"(Ini adalah contoh matriks yang sederhana namun luar biasa dan sering sangat berguna untuk dipertimbangkan.)\n"
"Ini tidak normal karena\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}^{\\dagger}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}^{\\dagger}\n"
"=\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "while\n"
msgstr "sementara\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}^{\\dagger}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}^{\\dagger}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Theorem statement {#theorem-statement}"
msgstr "Pernyataan teorema {#theorem-statement}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Now here's a statement of the spectral theorem.\n"
msgstr "Berikut adalah pernyataan teorema spektral.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Theorem\">\n"
"Spectral theorem: Let $M$ be a normal $N\\times N$ complex matrix.\n"
"There exists an orthonormal basis of $N$-dimensional complex vectors $\\bigl\\{ \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_N\\rangle \\bigr\\}$ along with complex numbers $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_N$ such that\n"
"$$\n"
"M = \\lambda_1 \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_1\\vert + \\cdots + \\lambda_N \\vert \\psi_N\\rangle\\langle \\psi_N\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Teorema\">\n"
"Teorema spektral: Misalkan $M$ adalah matriks kompleks $N\\times N$ yang normal.\n"
"Terdapat basis ortonormal dari vektor kompleks $N$-dimensi $\\bigl\\{ \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_N\\rangle \\bigr\\}$ bersama bilangan kompleks $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_N$ sedemikian sehingga\n"
"$$\n"
"M = \\lambda_1 \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_1\\vert + \\cdots + \\lambda_N \\vert \\psi_N\\rangle\\langle \\psi_N\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The expression of a matrix in the form\n"
msgstr "Ekspresi matriks dalam bentuk\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\sum_{k = 1}^N \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k\\vert \\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\sum_{k = 1}^N \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k\\vert \\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"is commonly called a *spectral decomposition*.\n"
"Notice that if $M$ is a normal matrix expressed in the form $(1),$ then the equation\n"
msgstr ""
"umumnya disebut sebagai *dekomposisi spektral*.\n"
"Perhatikan bahwa jika $M$ adalah matriks normal yang dinyatakan dalam bentuk $(1),$ maka persamaan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle = \\lambda_j \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle = \\lambda_j \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"must be true for every $j = 1,\\ldots,N.$\n"
"This is a consequence of the fact that $\\bigl\\{ \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_N\\rangle \\bigr\\}$ is orthonormal:\n"
msgstr ""
"harus benar untuk setiap $j = 1,\\ldots,N.$\n"
"Ini adalah konsekuensi dari fakta bahwa $\\bigl\\{ \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_N\\rangle \\bigr\\}$ adalah ortonormal:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"= \\left(\\sum_{k = 1}^N \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k\\vert\\right)\\vert \\psi_j\\rangle\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 1}^N \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k\\vert\\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"= \\lambda_j \\vert\\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"= \\left(\\sum_{k = 1}^N \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k\\vert\\right)\\vert \\psi_j\\rangle\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 1}^N \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k\\vert\\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"= \\lambda_j \\vert\\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"That is, each number $\\lambda_j$ is an *eigenvalue* of $M$ and "
"$\\vert\\psi_j\\rangle$ is an *eigenvector* corresponding to that "
"eigenvalue.\n"
msgstr ""
"Artinya, setiap bilangan $\\lambda_j$ adalah *eigenvalue* dari $M$ dan "
"$\\vert\\psi_j\\rangle$ adalah *eigenvector* yang bersesuaian dengan "
"eigenvalue tersebut.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Example 1**.\n"
"Let\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathbb{I} = \\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0\\\\0 & 1\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"**Contoh 1**.\n"
"Misalkan\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathbb{I} = \\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0\\\\0 & 1\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  which is normal.\n"
"  The theorem implies that $\\mathbb{I}$ can be written in the form $(1)$ for some choice of $\\lambda_1,$ $\\lambda_2,$ $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,$ and $\\vert\\psi_2\\rangle.$\n"
"  There are multiple choices that work, including\n"
msgstr ""
"  yang bersifat normal.\n"
"  Teorema menyiratkan bahwa $\\mathbb{I}$ dapat ditulis dalam bentuk $(1)$ untuk beberapa pilihan $\\lambda_1,$ $\\lambda_2,$ $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,$ dan $\\vert\\psi_2\\rangle.$\n"
"  Ada beberapa pilihan yang berhasil, termasuk\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\lambda_1 = 1, \\hspace{5pt}\n"
"  \\lambda_2 = 1, \\hspace{5pt}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle = \\vert 0\\rangle, \\hspace{5pt}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_2\\rangle = \\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\lambda_1 = 1, \\hspace{5pt}\n"
"  \\lambda_2 = 1, \\hspace{5pt}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle = \\vert 0\\rangle, \\hspace{5pt}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_2\\rangle = \\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Notice that the theorem does not say that the complex numbers $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_N$ are\n"
"  distinct — we can have the same complex number repeated, which is necessary for this example.\n"
"  These choices work because\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\mathbb{I} = \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert.\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  Perhatikan bahwa teorema tidak mengatakan bahwa bilangan kompleks $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_N$ berbeda — kita bisa memiliki bilangan kompleks yang sama berulang, yang diperlukan untuk contoh ini.\n"
"  Pilihan ini berhasil karena\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\mathbb{I} = \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert.\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Indeed, we could choose $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_2\\rangle\\}$ to be *any* orthonormal basis and the\n"
"  equation will be true. For instance,\n"
msgstr ""
"  Memang, kita bisa memilih $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_2\\rangle\\}$ sebagai basis ortonormal *manapun* dan\n"
"  persamaan akan benar. Misalnya,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\mathbb{I} = \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert + \\vert -\\rangle\\langle -\\vert.\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\mathbb{I} = \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert + \\vert -\\rangle\\langle -\\vert.\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Example 2**.\n"
"Consider a Hadamard operation.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Contoh 2**.\n"
"Pertimbangkan operasi Hadamard.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  H = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  1 & 1\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  1 & -1\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  H = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  1 & 1\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  1 & -1\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  This is a unitary matrix, so it is normal. The spectral theorem implies that $H$ can be written in the\n"
"  form $(1),$ and in particular we have\n"
msgstr ""
"  Ini adalah matriks uniter, sehingga bersifat normal. Teorema spektral menyiratkan bahwa $H$ dapat ditulis dalam\n"
"  bentuk $(1),$ dan khususnya kita memiliki\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  H =\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  - \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  H =\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  - \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "  where\n"
msgstr "  di mana\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle\n"
"  = \\cos(\\theta)\\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta) \\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle\n"
"  = \\cos(\\theta)\\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta) \\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "  More explicitly,\n"
msgstr "  Lebih eksplisit,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle, \\\\[3mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle & = -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"  \\end{aligned}\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle, \\\\[3mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle & = -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"  \\end{aligned}\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  We can check that this decomposition is correct by performing the required"
" calculations:\n"
msgstr ""
"  Kita bisa memeriksa bahwa dekomposisi ini benar dengan melakukan "
"perhitungan yang diperlukan:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  - \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"  -\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"  = H.\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  - \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"  -\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"  = H.\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As the first example above reveals, there can be some freedom in how eigenvectors are selected.\n"
"There is, however, no freedom at all in how the eigenvalues are chosen, except for their ordering:\n"
"the same $N$ complex numbers $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_N,$ which can include repetitions of the same complex number, will always occur in the equation $(1)$ for a given choice of a matrix $M.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Seperti yang diungkapkan contoh pertama di atas, bisa ada beberapa kebebasan dalam bagaimana eigenvector dipilih.\n"
"Namun, tidak ada kebebasan sama sekali dalam bagaimana eigenvalue dipilih, kecuali untuk urutannya:\n"
"bilangan kompleks $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_N$ yang sama, yang dapat mencakup pengulangan bilangan kompleks yang sama, akan selalu muncul dalam persamaan $(1)$ untuk pilihan matriks $M$ tertentu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's focus in on unitary matrices.\n"
"Suppose we have a complex number $\\lambda$ and a non-zero vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ that satisfy the equation\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang mari kita fokus pada matriks uniter.\n"
"Misalkan kita memiliki bilangan kompleks $\\lambda$ dan vektor non-nol $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ yang memenuhi persamaan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\lambda\\vert\\psi\\rangle.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\lambda\\vert\\psi\\rangle.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"That is, $\\lambda$ is an eigenvalue of $U$ and $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is an "
"eigenvector corresponding to this eigenvalue.\n"
msgstr ""
"Artinya, $\\lambda$ adalah eigenvalue dari $U$ dan $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ "
"adalah eigenvector yang bersesuaian dengan eigenvalue ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Unitary matrices preserve Euclidean norm, and so we conclude the following "
"from $(2).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Matriks uniter mempertahankan norma Euclidean, sehingga kita menyimpulkan "
"hal berikut dari $(2).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"= \\bigl\\| U \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"= \\bigl\\| \\lambda \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"= \\vert \\lambda \\vert \\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"= \\bigl\\| U \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"= \\bigl\\| \\lambda \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"= \\vert \\lambda \\vert \\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The condition that $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is non-zero implies that $\\bigl\\|"
" \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\\neq 0,$ so we can cancel it from both sides "
"to obtain\n"
msgstr ""
"Kondisi bahwa $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ adalah non-nol menyiratkan bahwa "
"$\\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\\neq 0,$ sehingga kita bisa "
"membatalkannya dari kedua sisi untuk mendapatkan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\lambda \\vert = 1.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\lambda \\vert = 1.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This reveals that eigenvalues of unitary matrices must always have absolute "
"value equal to one, so they lie on the *unit circle.*\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini mengungkapkan bahwa eigenvalue dari matriks uniter harus selalu memiliki"
" nilai absolut sama dengan satu, sehingga mereka berada pada *lingkaran "
"satuan.*\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathbb{T} = \\{\\alpha\\in\\mathbb{C} : \\vert\\alpha\\vert = 1\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathbb{T} = \\{\\alpha\\in\\mathbb{C} : \\vert\\alpha\\vert = 1\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(The symbol $\\mathbb{T}$ is a common name for the complex unit circle. The "
"name $S^1$ is also common.)\n"
msgstr ""
"(Simbol $\\mathbb{T}$ adalah nama umum untuk lingkaran satuan kompleks. Nama"
" $S^1$ juga umum.)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Phase estimation problem statement {#phase-estimation-problem-statement}"
msgstr ""
"Pernyataan masalah estimasi fase {#phase-estimation-problem-statement}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the *phase estimation problem*, we're given a quantum state $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ of $n$ qubits, along with a unitary quantum circuit that acts on $n$ qubits.\n"
"We're *promised* that $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ is an eigenvector of the unitary matrix $U$ that describes the action of the circuit, and our goal is to compute or approximate the eigenvalue $\\lambda$ to which $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ corresponds.\n"
"More precisely, because $\\lambda$ lies on the complex unit circle, we can write\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam *masalah estimasi fase*, kita diberikan keadaan kuantum $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ dari $n$ qubit, bersama sirkuit kuantum uniter yang bertindak pada $n$ qubit.\n"
"Kita *dijanjikan* bahwa $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ adalah eigenvector dari matriks uniter $U$ yang mendeskripsikan aksi sirkuit, dan tujuan kita adalah menghitung atau mendekati eigenvalue $\\lambda$ yang bersesuaian dengan $\\vert \\psi\\rangle.$\n"
"Lebih tepatnya, karena $\\lambda$ berada pada lingkaran satuan kompleks, kita dapat menulis\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\lambda = e^{2\\pi i \\theta}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\lambda = e^{2\\pi i \\theta}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for a unique real number $\\theta$ satisfying $0\\leq\\theta<1.$\n"
"The goal of the problem is to compute or approximate this real number $\\theta.$\n"
msgstr ""
"untuk bilangan real unik $\\theta$ yang memenuhi $0\\leq\\theta<1.$\n"
"Tujuan masalah adalah menghitung atau mendekati bilangan real $\\theta$ ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Phase estimation problem\">\n"
"Input: A unitary quantum circuit for an $n$-qubit operation $U$ along with an $n$-qubit quantum state $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ \\\n"
"Promise: $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is an eigenvector of $U$ \\\n"
"Output: an approximation to the number $\\theta\\in[0,1)$ satisfying $U\\vert\\psi\\rangle = e^{2\\pi i \\theta}\\vert\\psi\\rangle$\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Masalah estimasi fase\">\n"
"Input: Sirkuit kuantum uniter untuk operasi $U$ $n$-qubit bersama keadaan kuantum $n$-qubit $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ \\\n"
"Janji: $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ adalah eigenvector dari $U$ \\\n"
"Output: aproksimasi untuk bilangan $\\theta\\in[0,1)$ yang memenuhi $U\\vert\\psi\\rangle = e^{2\\pi i \\theta}\\vert\\psi\\rangle$\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Here are a few remarks about this problem statement:\n"
msgstr "Berikut adalah beberapa catatan tentang pernyataan masalah ini:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The phase estimation problem is different from other problems we've seen so "
"far in the course in that the input includes a quantum state. Typically we "
"focus on problems having classical inputs and outputs, but nothing prevents "
"us from considering quantum state inputs like this. In terms of its "
"practical relevance, the phase estimation problem is typically encountered "
"as a *subproblem* inside of a larger computation, like we'll see in the "
"context of integer factorization later in the lesson.\n"
msgstr ""
"Masalah estimasi fase berbeda dari masalah lain yang sudah kita lihat sejauh"
" ini dalam kursus karena inputnya mencakup keadaan kuantum. Biasanya kita "
"fokus pada masalah yang memiliki input dan output klasik, tetapi tidak ada "
"yang mencegah kita mempertimbangkan input keadaan kuantum seperti ini. Dalam"
" hal relevansi praktisnya, masalah estimasi fase biasanya ditemui sebagai "
"*submasalah* di dalam komputasi yang lebih besar, seperti yang akan kita "
"lihat dalam konteks faktorisasi bilangan bulat nanti dalam pelajaran.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The statement of the phase estimation problem above isn't specific about "
"what constitutes an approximation of $\\theta,$ but we can formulate more "
"precise problem statements depending on our needs and interests. In the "
"context of integer factorization, we'll demand a very precise approximation "
"to $\\theta,$ but in other cases we might be satisfied with a very rough "
"approximation. We'll discuss shortly how the precision we require affects "
"the computational cost of a solution.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pernyataan masalah estimasi fase di atas tidak spesifik tentang apa yang "
"merupakan aproksimasi dari $\\theta,$ tetapi kita dapat merumuskan "
"pernyataan masalah yang lebih tepat tergantung pada kebutuhan dan minat "
"kita. Dalam konteks faktorisasi bilangan bulat, kita akan menuntut "
"aproksimasi yang sangat tepat untuk $\\theta,$ tetapi dalam kasus lain kita "
"mungkin puas dengan aproksimasi yang sangat kasar. Kita akan membahas segera"
" bagaimana presisi yang kita butuhkan mempengaruhi biaya komputasi dari "
"solusi.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Notice that as we go from $\\theta = 0$ toward $\\theta = 1$ in the phase "
"estimation problem, we're going all the way around the unit circle, starting"
" from $e^{2\\pi i \\cdot 0} = 1$ and moving counter-clockwise toward "
"$e^{2\\pi i \\cdot 1} = 1.$ That is, when we reach $\\theta = 1$ we're back "
"where we started at $\\theta = 0.$ So, as we consider the accuracy of "
"approximations, choices of $\\theta$ near $1$ should be considered as being "
"near $0.$ For example, an approximation $\\theta = 0.999$ should be "
"considered as being within $1/1000$ of $\\theta = 0.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa saat kita bergerak dari $\\theta = 0$ menuju $\\theta = 1$ "
"dalam masalah estimasi fase, kita mengelilingi seluruh lingkaran satuan, "
"mulai dari $e^{2\\pi i \\cdot 0} = 1$ dan bergerak berlawanan arah jarum jam"
" menuju $e^{2\\pi i \\cdot 1} = 1.$ Artinya, ketika kita mencapai $\\theta ="
" 1$ kita kembali ke tempat mulai di $\\theta = 0.$ Jadi, saat kita "
"mempertimbangkan akurasi aproksimasi, pilihan $\\theta$ yang mendekati $1$ "
"harus dianggap sebagai dekat dengan $0.$ Misalnya, aproksimasi $\\theta = "
"0.999$ harus dianggap berada dalam $1/1000$ dari $\\theta = 0.$\n"
